*> Acceptance test of docs/protocol/42-particles-1-shared-model-engine.md section 3 (particle options and
*> their forms): the wire layout of every options class (block, item template, colour, dust, dust
*> transition, spell, power, shriek, sculk charge, vibration, trail, geysers, explosion info), the
*> scale clamp, the colour getters, the constants, the JSON defaults and ranges, the particle limit.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-PARTICLES-42-1-3.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY CLPART.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAP                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 256.
 01 WS-INT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLOAT               FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 WS-DOUBLE              FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(160).
 01 WS-CONST               PIC X(24).
 01 WS-MSG                 PIC X(64).
 01 WS-A                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-R                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-G                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-B                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-PACKED              BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-SCALED              BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LIMIT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SCALING             FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-SPEED               FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-TWO                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 2.
 01 WS-CMP                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAP
*>   block (id 1) : VarInt block state id.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 5000 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PART-OPT-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID PART-OPTIONS
     MOVE "block: kind" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM TEXT-CASE-KIND
     MOVE "block: state id" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 5000 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PO-BLOCK-STATE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-NUMBER
     MOVE "block: read position" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PB-POS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-NUMBER
*>   Block state outside the registry is an error (registry size 5000 -> id 5000 is out).
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 5000 TO PO-BLOCK-STATE-COUNT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PART-OPT-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID PART-OPTIONS
     MOVE "block: id outside the registry is an error" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PO-ERROR TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-NUMBER
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 4999 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PART-OPT-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID PART-OPTIONS
     MOVE "block: last registry id is valid" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PO-ERROR TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     PERFORM ASSERT-NUMBER
*>   falling_dust (36), dust_pillar (121), block_crumble (125), block_marker (2) share the layout.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-ID FROM 36 BY 85 UNTIL WS-ID > 125
         CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
         CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
         MOVE 0 TO PO-BLOCK-STATE-COUNT
         CALL "PART-OPT-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID PART-OPTIONS
         MOVE "block layout shared by ids 36 and 121: state id" TO WS-NAME
         MOVE 4999 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE PO-BLOCK-STATE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         PERFORM ASSERT-NUMBER
     END-PERFORM
*>   item (57): ItemStackTemplate = item id, count, empty patch.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE 57 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 812 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-INT
     CALL "PART-OPT-DECODE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ID PART-OPTIONS
     MOVE "item: item id" TO WS-NAME
